<title>UK: Rain seen in eastern England grain area on Friday.</title>
<headline>Rain seen in eastern England grain area on Friday.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eastern England is likely to get some rain during the course of Friday, a spokesman for the Meteorological Office said.</p>
<p>Developing cereals in eastern England, including the important grain producing area of East Anglia, have suffered most from the prolonged dry spell.</p>
<p>Another belt of rain will cross the country on Sunday, followed by showers next week, the spokesman said. Showery conditions, however, are more likely to benefit the north and west, than the south and east.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a change in the weather pattern over the next five days,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;The difficult question is still the amount of rain,&quot; he said. But the indications were that &quot;most parts will see measurable rain, rather than the spots we've seen over the past few days.&quot;</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
